# What must never be sent to the Docker daemon as build context.
#
# node_modules and dist are the big ones: `npm ci` installs the tree inside the image and
# `npm run build` writes dist there, so copying either from the host would be slow and, with
# node_modules built for Windows, wrong. .env.local is a secrets file and the build gets its
# VITE_* values as build arguments instead.

# Local environment files. .env.example is a committed template and is harmless.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Installed and built output: the image produces both itself.
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
coverage

# Git history and local tooling.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.idea
.vscode

# Documentation and design sources: not part of the bundle.
*.md
docs/
design/

# Logs.
*.log
